 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Generally yes, but it' a bit like reading a foreign book. Many words are the same, but the whole thing flows differently. The grammar can be strange. For example, the ing form of verbs is added differently, there are different tenses, and some words don't exist. It is, once you get used to it. The big thing is the vocabulary. Some sounds are different, like the s sound in English is different from the z sound in Dutch. Watching a show in your native language is easier, reading a book in the same language is easier still. Then watch some Norwegian TV with subtitles. It' a great way to practice.",
